Package: easyTSA
Title: Trial Sequential Analysis for 'meta' Objects
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R:
    person("Vanio", "Antunes", email = "vanio.antunes.md@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Runs Trial Sequential Analysis (TSA) on meta-analysis objects
    created with the 'meta' package by driving the Copenhagen Trial Unit TSA
    program itself: the trials are written to the program's '.TSA' file, the
    program (downloaded from its authors by tsa_setup(), never bundled, run
    headlessly through 'rJava') computes
    the required information size, cumulative Z-curve, monitoring and
    futility boundaries and heterogeneity, and the results come back to R
    as a tidy object with a 'ggplot2' plot. No statistic is recomputed in R.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    meta (>= 6.0.0),
    rJava,
    rJavaEnv (>= 0.3.0),
    ggplot2,
    stats,
    tools,
    utils
SystemRequirements: TSA 0.9.5.10 Beta from https://ctu.dk/tools (downloaded
    by tsa_setup(), not bundled); Java (>= 8), installed by tsa_setup() when
    missing
Suggests:
    readxl,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
